## Testing Recommendations

1. **Verify rejection works**: Test with a disallowed origin (should see CORS error)
2. **Verify allowlist works**: Set CORS_ALLOWLIST and test with allowed origins
3. **Verify development mode**: Test localhost access works without env vars
4. **Verify production safety**: Test that unknown origins are rejected in production mode

## Security Impact

This change closes a critical security gap identified in the assessment. Previously, ALL origins were allowed in production (line 31: `callback(null, true)`). Now, only explicitly configured origins can access the API, preventing cross-origin attacks from malicious websites.

## Migration Notes for Deployment

When deploying to production (Render/Railway/Vercel), ensure you set:
```bash
CORS_ALLOWLIST=https://your-frontend-domain.com,https://www.anthropic.com
```

Or for single origin:
```bash
FRONTEND_URL=https://your-frontend-domain.com
```
